-- DICT-SEMANTICS §6.1 choice-point 2, THE SEPARATING CASE the spec names in its
-- own text: "`C (Pair Int a)`, `C (Pair a Int)`, `C (Pair Int Int)` all declared.
-- At the goal `C (Pair Int Int)` the first two are INCOMPARABLE, but the third is
-- ⊑ both -- (c) ACCEPTS WITH AN UNAMBIGUOUS WINNER; (a)/(b) reject."
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (HAND-DERIVED FROM §3 `match` AND §3 ⊑, NOT CAPTURED). This value was
-- worked out before F-3d existed and is unchanged by it -- the file's previous
-- header already carried it, as the answer the implementation was DIVERGING from:
--   `match(IE, C (Pair Int Int))` = all three heads. `Pair Int Int` is an instance
--   of `Pair Int a` (a↦Int) and of `Pair a Int` (a↦Int), and neither of those two is
--   an instance of the other (no substitution on `a` turns `Pair Int a` into
--   `Pair a Int`, since `Int` is not a variable). So `Pair Int Int` is ⊑ every
--   element and is the UNIQUE ⊑-minimum. §3 `inst` = min⊑(match) selects it, and
--   `cname (MkPair 1 1)` prints **3**. §6.1: "Recommended: (c) as the semantics ...
--   An implementation MAY ADDITIONALLY WARN at declaration time on (a)-violations as
--   an early diagnostic, BUT ACCEPTANCE IS PER-GOAL."
--
-- OBSERVED (F-3d, #614/#311 -- THE DRAIN): check/run/build all ACCEPT and both
-- engines print 3. The declaration-time (a) sweep still fires, DEMOTED to the
-- `W-INCOMPARABLE-IMPLS` warning §6.1 licenses, naming the ⊑-incomparable pair
-- `Pair a Int` / `Pair Int b`. CONFORMANT on verdict, value AND diagnostic class.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS ROW WAS PINNED TO THE REJECT UNTIL 2026-08-01 (as
-- s6-1c-per-goal-unique-min-REJECTED.mdk). It is renamed rather than re-labelled
-- because a fixture whose NAME asserts the opposite of what it now tests is the
-- rot this corpus exists to prevent. Its must-fail twin
-- (test/must_fail_fixtures/614-coherence-global-comparability/) drained in the same
-- change and was deleted.
--
-- ⚠️ WHAT DID **NOT** WIDEN, and the reason it is worth knowing here: F-3d demotes
-- condition (a) ONLY. Two MUTUALLY-⊑ (α-equal) heads still hard-reject with
-- `T-CONFLICTING-IMPL` -- they SATISFY (a) (they are ⊑-comparable) while violating
-- §6 C1 outright (two ⊑-minimal elements, so no minimum), and `entryCovers` makes
-- equal heads cover each other, so the goal-site reject cannot see them either.
-- s6-c1-duplicate-heads-rejected.mdk is that control and is unchanged.
--
-- The DISCRIMINATING CONTROL for this row is s6-1c-incomparable-no-minimum-control:
-- the same program with the third impl DELETED. It still REJECTS -- now at the GOAL,
-- with T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE -- so "adding the unique ⊑-minimum rescues the program"
-- is an observed difference between two files rather than a claim about one.
data Pair a b = MkPair a b

interface C a where
  cname : a -> Int

impl C (Pair Int a) where
  cname _ = 1

impl C (Pair a Int) where
  cname _ = 2

impl C (Pair Int Int) where
  cname _ = 3

main = println (cname (MkPair 1 1))
